.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-check
.Nd check a sealed capsule folder against its seal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis check
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Op Fl -anchor Ar der-file ...
.Op Fl -only Ar path ...
.Op Fl -lineage Ar input-dir ...
.Op Fl -keys Ar file ...
.Ar dir | url
.Nm noqtis check
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Op Fl -anchor Ar der-file ...
.Fl -proof Ar file | url
.Op Ar dir | url
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis check
checks the capsule
.Ar dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5 :
it reads and checks the seal
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
checks that the SHA-256 of
.Pa noqtis.json
is the one in the seal, verifies the signature over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json ,
then lists the folder and checks every listed file (present, a regular
file, the size, the SHA-256 and the SHA3-256) and that no file is present
that the manifest does not list.
.Pp
It prints one row per check: a status
.Pq Ql ok No or Ql FAIL ,
the check's name and a detail, then a summary line
.Dl <dir>: OK (<n> checks passed)
or
.Dl <dir>: FAILED (<k> of <n> checks failed)
.Pp
Without
.Fl p ,
the public key inside the seal is accepted: the check then shows that the
files are those the key holder sealed, not who the key holder is.
The
.Ql key
row says so, and a note on standard error says to pass
.Fl p .
With
.Fl p ,
the seal's key must be exactly the given key, and the seal's algorithm
the one the key file names (a
.Ql key.alg
row fails otherwise).
Each option that takes a value may be given once.
.Pp
Files are opened folder by folder from
.Ar dir ,
never through a link, so a folder swapped for a link while the check runs
fails it instead of being followed.
A listed file whose size differs is reported without being read, and no
file is read past one byte more than its listed size.
File names and other text from the folder or a TSA are printed with
control characters escaped
.Pq Ql \ex1b ,
so they cannot rewrite the terminal.
.Pp
With
.Fl -anchor ,
the seal must carry an RFC 3161 timestamp over its signature whose token
verifies under one of the anchors, with the TSA certificate's path valid
at the token's genTime; the
.Ql timestamp
row then shows the genTime.
Without
.Fl -anchor ,
a seal that carries a timestamp fails its
.Ql timestamp
row: a timestamp that cannot be checked is never passed silently.
.Pp
Given a
.Ar url
.Pq Ql http:// , or Ql https:// No when noqtis was built with its TLS client
in place of a folder, the capsule served there is checked: the URL of the
folder that holds
.Pa noqtis.sig
and
.Pa noqtis.json
on the server, without a query or fragment.
Both are fetched into a new temporary folder and checked first, against
.Fl p
and the anchors when given; only when the seal, its signature and the
manifest check are the listed files fetched (with
.Fl -only ,
only those), each by its path under the URL, percent-encoded, and at most
its listed size, a file over 1 GiB or past the 10000th not at all.
The folder is then checked as any other, so a file the server lacks or
changed fails its row, and everything written to it is removed after.
The report names the URL.
Redirects are followed, at most five, never from
.Ql https://
to
.Ql http:// .
A
.Fl -proof
may also be a URL.
.Pp
After the table, for each failed check, a line on standard error says
what to do:
.Dl noqtis check: Ar check : Ar what to do
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
The public signature key the capsule must be sealed with.
.It Fl j , Fl -json
Print one line of JSON instead of the table:
.Bd -literal
{"capsule":"<dir>","ok":<bool>,"result":"<nqerr text>",
 "checks":[{"check":"<name>","ok":<bool>,"detail":"<text>"},...]}
.Ed
.Pp
A failed check also has
.Ql fix ,
the text of the line on standard error.
.It Fl -anchor Ar der-file
A TSA trust anchor: the root or issuing certificate of a time-stamping
authority, DER-encoded (convert PEM with
.Ql openssl x509 -outform DER ) .
Up to 32; one that verifies the token is enough.
.It Fl -only Ar path
Check only this listed file, up to 32 times: a partial check.
The seal, the signature and the whole manifest are still checked; files
not named are neither read nor needed, and files present but not listed
are not looked for.
.Ql partial
rows say so, so a partial pass is never mistaken for a full one.
A named path the manifest does not list fails its
.Ql file
row.
.It Fl -lineage Ar input-dir
The folder of a capsule that may be one of the inputs of
.Ar dir
(a format 2 capsule sealed with
.Xr noqtis-seal 1
.Fl -input ) ,
up to 32 times.
Each input is found among them by its id, the SHA-256 of the bytes its
seal signs, and checked in full without a pinned key; its own inputs are
looked for in the same folders, to 64 levels.
One
.Ql lineage
row per input says whether it was found and checks.
.It Fl -proof Ar file
Check a proof made by
.Xr noqtis-prove 1
instead of a folder: the seal in the proof, its signature over the
manifest's head, and each proven entry's Merkle audit path to the root
the head signs
.Pq Ql proof.entry .
With
.Ar dir ,
the proven files there are also checked against their entries, and a
.Ql partial
row says the capsule's other files are not in the proof.
.Fl -only ,
.Fl -lineage
and
.Fl -keys
do not apply.
.It Fl -keys Ar file
A key statement from
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1
or
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
up to 32 times; it needs
.Fl p .
The statements are followed from the
.Fl p
key: a seal made with a key it was rotated to passes the
.Ql key
row, and one made with a key since rotated away or revoked passes only
when a verified timestamp
.Pq Fl -anchor
shows it was sealed before then
.Pq Ql key.time .
One
.Ql keys
row per statement; two statements about one key, or a rotation back to
an earlier key, trust no key.
.El
.Ss Checks
The row names are stable, for scripts:
.Bl -tag -width "manifest.canonical"
.It Cm seal.read
.Pa noqtis.sig
exists, is a regular file (not a link) and is at most 1 MiB.
.It Cm seal.parse , seal.canonical
It is a JSON object in canonical form (RFC 8785).
.It Cm seal.fields
It has exactly the fields of
.Ql noqtis-seal-1 ,
with the right types;
.Ql manifest_sha256
is 64 lower-case hex digits.
.It Cm seal.format
.Ql format
is
.Ql noqtis-seal-1 .
.It Cm seal.alg
.Ql alg
names a signature algorithm noqtis knows.
.It Cm seal.context
.Ql context
is at most 255 bytes.
.It Cm seal.key , seal.signature
.Ql public_key
and
.Ql signature
are base64 of the algorithm's sizes.
.It Cm manifest.read
.Pa noqtis.json
exists, is a regular file and is at most 512 MiB.
.It Cm manifest.digest
Its SHA-256 is the seal's
.Ql manifest_sha256 .
.It Cm key
Whether the key was pinned with
.Fl p .
.It Cm signature
The signature verifies over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json .
.It Cm timestamp
Present only when the seal has a timestamp or
.Fl -anchor
was given.
.It Cm folder
The folder could be listed within the limits.
.It Cm file
One row per listed file.
.It Cm manifest.parse , manifest.canonical , manifest.fields
The manifest is canonical JSON with exactly the fields of
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 .
.It Cm manifest.format , manifest.created , manifest.order
.Ql format
is
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1
(or
.Ql noqtis-capsule-2
under a
.Ql noqtis-seal-2
seal),
.Ql created
is an RFC 3339 UTC time, and the files are sorted by path with no repeats.
.It Cm manifest.merkle
Format 2: the Merkle tree over the file entries has the root and leaf
count the signed head gives.
.It Cm lineage
With
.Fl -lineage :
one row per input of the capsule.
.It Cm keys
With
.Fl -keys :
one row per statement, and its signatures.
.It Cm key.time
With
.Fl -keys ,
when the seal's key was rotated away or revoked: the verified
timestamp's genTime is before then.
.It Cm partial
With
.Fl -only
or
.Fl -proof :
what the check left out; never a failure.
.It Cm proof.parse , proof.canonical , proof.fields , proof.entry
With
.Fl -proof :
the proof is canonical JSON with exactly the fields of
.Ql noqtis-proof-1 ,
and each entry's audit path leads to the signed root.
.It Cm path
One row per refused, non-normal, duplicate or too long path, and per two
paths that differ only in case.
.It Cm extra
One row per regular file present but not listed.
.It Cm unsafe
One row per link, reparse point, special file or refused name in the
folder.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SSL_CERT_FILE
For an
.Ql https://
.Ar url :
a PEM bundle of the roots to trust, in place of the system's.
.It Ev NOQTIS_CT_LOGS
For an
.Ql https://
.Ar url :
a Certificate Transparency log list in the form of Chrome's
.Pa log_list.json
(version 3), such as
.Lk https://www.gstatic.com/ct/log_list/v3/log_list.json .
When it is set, the server's certificate must carry SCTs (embedded, or
sent in TLS) that verify and come from logs of at least two operators,
usable when they signed; otherwise the fetch fails and says why.
Unset or empty, nothing is checked: a list goes stale, so keep it
current.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
Every check passed.
.It 1
A check failed (the files changed, the seal or manifest is damaged or not
signed by
.Ar key.pub ) .
.It 2
A usage error,
.Ar dir
does not exist, a key that is not a public signature key, an anchor that
cannot be read or is not DER, or a library error such as running out of
memory.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results
      check               detail
ok    seal.read           noqtis.sig
\&...
ok    signature           ML-DSA-65 signature over noqtis.json is valid
ok    folder              listed
ok    file                data/in.csv
ok    file                report.txt
\&...
ok    manifest.order      files sorted by path, no repeats
results: OK (22 checks passed)
.Ed
.Pp
After a file was changed and one added:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub results; echo $?
\&...
FAIL  file                report.txt: size differs
\&...
FAIL  extra               new.txt: not in the manifest
results: FAILED (2 of 23 checks failed)
noqtis check: file: a sealed file changed after sealing: restore it from the original, or seal the folder again if the change was intended
noqtis check: extra: a file was added after sealing: remove it, or seal the folder again to include it
1
.Ed
.Pp
A timestamped capsule, against the TSA's root certificate:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --anchor digicert.der results
\&...
ok    timestamp           RFC 3161 token over the signature verifies under a TSA anchor; genTime 2026-10-29T09:34:03Z
\&...
results: OK (23 checks passed)
.Ed
.Pp
A capsule published on a web server, without downloading it by hand:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub https://example.org/data/results/
.Ed
.Pp
Only one file of a format 2 capsule, and its inputs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --only data/in.csv results
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --lineage raw results
.Ed
.Pp
In CI, keeping only the failed rows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis check --json -p me.pub results |
    jq -r '.checks[] | select(.ok | not) | .detail'
report.txt: size differs
new.txt: not in the manifest
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-prove 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqchkt 3 ,
.Xr nqtsput 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
